      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #64, 2026-08-11): ⍸B on a rank
      ⍝ ≥ 2 empty or all-zero B had a simple prototype -- eval_B's final
      ⍝ Z->set_proto_Int() (Bif_F12_INTERVAL_INDEX.cc) sets a plain IntCell
      ⍝ 0 regardless of B's rank, instead of a pointer to a rank-item zero
      ⍝ vector (matching a real item, per the "nested shape" branch just
      ⍝ above it), so ≡Z came out 1 (want 2) and ⍴↑Z came out ⍬ (want the
      ⍝ item shape, here 2).
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⍤ ⍣ ⍸ ≢ are not in IBM APL2
      Z←⍸2 2⍴0 ⋄ ≡Z ⋄ ⍴↑Z
2
2

      ⍝ control: the non-empty case was already right
      ⍝
      Z←⍸2 2⍴1 ⋄ ≡Z ⋄ ⍴↑Z
2
2

