      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(r)): A⍸B used to order genuinely complex
      ⍝ numbers silently via Cell::compare()'s arbitrary real-then-
      ⍝ imaginary fallback (e.g. 1J1 2⍸1 gave 0 instead of a DOMAIN
      ⍝ ERROR), unlike ⍋/⍒ (Bif_F12_SORT::sort()), which already rejects
      ⍝ exactly this with the same can_be_compared() check now used here.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⍤ ⍣ ⍸ ≢ are not in IBM APL2
      0J1 2⍸1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      0J1 2⍸1
      ^    ^

      )MORE
A⍸B: A contains items that cannot be compared with each other
      )SIC

      1 2⍸0J1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      1 2⍸0J1
      ^  ^

      )MORE
A⍸B: B contains items that cannot be compared with each other
      )SIC

